{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778517540866,"sessionID":"ses_1e8183fceffenG367CcnNzvwcT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-abcfd0f7ad763ad1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**CL term**\\n[CL_0000999](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000999) — CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell\\n\\n**Suggested revision of class hierarchy**\\nChange the Equivalent To class from `conventional dendritic cell` to [CD11b-positive dendritic cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002465).\\n\\n**Rationale**  \\nCurrently, CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell (CL_0000999) has `conventional dendritic cell` as its Equivalent To class. We propose changing it to CD11b-positive dendritic cell. This change reflects a more natural hierarchical relationship, as CD11b-positive dendritic cell represents a parent concept encompassing CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell.\\n\\nA concrete example supporting this change is already present in the ontology: CD4-negative, CD8-alpha-negative, CD11b-positive dendritic cell (CL_0002454) uses CD11b-positive dendritic cell as its Equivalent To class. Applying the same principle here ensures consistency and aligns with existing ontology modeling practices.\\n\\nThank you for your consideration.\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"[Class hierarchy] CD4+ CD11b+ dendritic cell [CL_0000999]: Change parent to CD11b+ DC\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3379\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**CL term**\\n[CL_0000999](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000999) — CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell\\n\\n**Suggested revision of class hierarchy**\\nChange the Equivalent To class from `conventional dendritic cell` to [CD11b-positive dendritic cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002465).\\n\\n**Rationale**  \\nCurrently, CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell (CL_0000999) has `conventional dendritic cell` as its Equivalent To class. We propose changing it to CD11b-positive dendritic cell. This change reflects a more natural hierarchical relationship, as CD11b-positive dendritic cell represents a parent concept encompassing CD4-positive CD11b-positive dendritic cell.\\n\\nA concrete example supporting this change is already present in the ontology: CD4-negative, CD8-alpha-negative, CD11b-positive dendritic cell (CL_0002454) uses CD11b-positive dendritic cell as its Equivalent To class. Applying the same principle here ensures consistency and aligns with existing ontology modeling practices.\\n\\nThank you for your consideration.\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"[Class hierarchy] CD4+ CD11b+ dendritic cell [CL_0000999]: Change parent to CD11b+ DC\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3379\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778517540849,"end":1778517540864}},"id":"prt_e17e7fc1a001O0DjrsW24uP5z0","sessionID":"ses_1e8183fceffenG367CcnNzvwcT","messageID":"msg_e17e7c0e90012b51bllUqbo3NU"}}
